WEBVTT

00:07.133 --> 00:08.967
Hi, this is
Robbie Robertson calling.

00:08.968 --> 00:11.136
Mr. Robertson,
you're never getting your old job back.

00:11.137 --> 00:12.929
I'm onto something truly sensational!

00:12.930 --> 00:17.851
Three POWs from the same camp
with super abilities isn't a coincidence.

00:17.852 --> 00:20.603
The only thing
Silvermane gets off on is power.

00:20.604 --> 00:21.480
If he gave it to me...

00:22.314 --> 00:23.648
...then he can take it all away.

00:23.649 --> 00:25.358
They did something
to you all, didn't they?

00:25.359 --> 00:28.445
All I know is that once it starts,
it gets worse fast.

00:28.446 --> 00:30.280
But you should talk to Doc Faber.

00:30.281 --> 00:32.532
She can explain what's going on
a whole lot better than I can.

00:32.533 --> 00:34.993
One of those super freaks
is tearing up the Diamond District.

00:34.994 --> 00:36.369
The Spider is there.

00:37.997 --> 00:39.581
Who the hell is this guy?

00:43.043 --> 00:45.420
- Me and The Spider have teamed up...
-  Not-not a team.

00:45.421 --> 00:47.839
- ...to save this city!
- Not a team. No, not a team.

00:47.840 --> 00:51.676
Every four years,
I decide who sits in your chair.

00:51.677 --> 00:53.429
I'm not backing down.

01:00.394 --> 01:03.397
Nice to meet you, Mr. Spider.

01:16.118 --> 01:18.453
♪ You turned the tables ♪

01:18.454 --> 01:21.790
- ♪ on me ♪
- Hey, come on.

01:21.791 --> 01:23.625
Hey.

01:23.626 --> 01:25.877
♪ And now I'm falling for you ♪

01:25.878 --> 01:28.755
Hey, lady, what's your hurry?

01:28.756 --> 01:32.468
♪ You turned the tables on me ♪

01:34.553 --> 01:36.679
♪ I can't believe ♪

01:36.680 --> 01:39.140
- ♪ that it's true ♪
-  Here, here, let me get the door.

01:39.141 --> 01:40.934
After you.

01:40.935 --> 01:42.602
♪ I always thought ♪

01:42.603 --> 01:45.605
♪ when you brought the lovely present...

01:45.606 --> 01:46.982
So...

01:48.067 --> 01:49.484
So, yourself.

01:49.485 --> 01:51.569
We're about
to turn over the pies.

01:51.570 --> 01:53.947
This one's on the house.

01:53.948 --> 01:56.116
What, more of a blueberry guy?

01:56.700 --> 02:00.245
No, there's just not a lot of free stuff
going around these days.

02:00.246 --> 02:01.579
Thank you.

02:01.580 --> 02:02.998
Very kind.

02:04.583 --> 02:05.875
♪ You let me fall...

02:05.876 --> 02:08.045
I'm waiting, you know.

02:08.629 --> 02:11.005
You already know how it ends.

02:11.006 --> 02:14.093
Well, then start from the beginning.

02:18.722 --> 02:22.935
We were sent to liberate
a small town in Eastern France.

02:23.435 --> 02:26.521
The Germans weren't so keen
on giving it up.

02:37.366 --> 02:38.242
Move, move, move!

02:41.745 --> 02:43.747
Scheiße.

02:45.124 --> 02:46.624
Charge!

03:34.840 --> 03:36.675
Jones. Jones!

03:37.259 --> 03:38.801
Get 'em out!

03:38.802 --> 03:40.011
- Get 'em out.
-  Please.

03:40.012 --> 03:41.889
- Private, follow me.
- Yes, sir.

03:42.556 --> 03:44.015
Move.

03:44.016 --> 03:45.099
Let's go.

03:45.100 --> 03:47.435
If I was the one who had been shot,

03:47.436 --> 03:49.395
and I almost was,

03:49.396 --> 03:53.024
none of this would have happened to me.

03:53.025 --> 03:54.943
I think about that a lot.

04:06.038 --> 04:09.416
Private Smith and I pressed deeper
into the compound.

04:14.129 --> 04:15.463
Jesus.

04:15.464 --> 04:16.798
Let's get 'em out of here.

04:16.799 --> 04:17.800
Help me.

04:45.494 --> 04:46.869
You okay, pal?

04:46.870 --> 04:48.706
I'm gonna get you out of here.

04:58.841 --> 05:00.466
Are you okay?

05:00.467 --> 05:03.387
Reilly.

05:04.388 --> 05:05.805
Are you okay?

05:05.806 --> 05:07.766
Sarge, Sarge!

05:19.820 --> 05:21.612
Sarge!

05:21.613 --> 05:23.239
- What do we do?
- Burn it.

05:23.240 --> 05:24.407
Burn it all.

05:30.080 --> 05:31.457
Ready.

05:35.044 --> 05:36.170
Ready.

05:37.463 --> 05:40.924
One, two, three.

05:54.480 --> 05:57.148
♪ The colors fading from the photograph ♪

05:57.149 --> 05:58.900
♪ I could tell the story ♪

05:58.901 --> 06:01.569
♪ but still you wouldn't know the half ♪

06:01.570 --> 06:04.363
♪ This love was brought to life
from shards of glass ♪

06:04.364 --> 06:06.449
♪ When you kiss me there's a shifting ♪

06:06.450 --> 06:08.910
♪ in the sepia tone ♪

06:08.911 --> 06:12.121
♪ Can't escape the madness,
baby, magnetism ♪

06:12.122 --> 06:15.458
♪ Run away but something
pulls me back into it ♪

06:15.459 --> 06:18.586
♪ Lately I've been staring
at a broken mirror ♪

06:18.587 --> 06:22.048
♪ Needing someone to call my own ♪

06:22.049 --> 06:25.259
♪ Hey, lover ♪

06:25.260 --> 06:28.137
♪ I need someone to save me now ♪

06:28.138 --> 06:30.389
♪ from all the pain ♪

06:30.390 --> 06:32.850
♪ I suffer ♪

06:32.851 --> 06:35.686
♪ and the heavy world
that weighs me down ♪

06:35.687 --> 06:39.232
♪ 'Cause the world ain't sweet ♪

06:39.233 --> 06:41.609
♪ It's bitter to taste ♪

06:41.610 --> 06:42.985
♪ But you could be ♪

06:42.986 --> 06:46.198
♪ my saving grace ♪

07:12.432 --> 07:14.100
And that was it?

07:14.101 --> 07:15.268
After that you were...?

07:20.566 --> 07:21.775
Yes.

07:23.569 --> 07:29.116
It took some time at first just to relearn
how to be more human again.

07:30.117 --> 07:33.244
Believe it or not, I went to the movies,
I watched the actors,

07:33.245 --> 07:38.458
I studied the way they spoke,
the way they moved.

07:41.837 --> 07:44.922
The arachnid genes are still in me.

07:44.923 --> 07:50.971
The tics, the... thoughts, impulses.

07:52.097 --> 07:55.184
But I manage to suppress them.

07:56.977 --> 07:58.645
Most of the time.

08:00.314 --> 08:02.733
You once told me you were a coward.

08:03.775 --> 08:06.028
And to think I almost believed you.

08:10.282 --> 08:14.076
If Flint was there, his powers
must have come from the same place.

08:14.077 --> 08:16.412
Hard to think otherwise.

08:16.413 --> 08:18.080
Is that the real reason you took the case?

08:18.081 --> 08:19.081
Yes.

08:19.082 --> 08:24.003
In part, but, yes, I-I did it because
I wanted to learn something from Flint.

08:24.004 --> 08:29.508
If something gave both of us these powers,
maybe something could take 'em back.

08:29.509 --> 08:32.053
Would you really want that?

08:32.054 --> 08:33.679
Lose all your powers?

08:33.680 --> 08:37.475
Go back to being just... Ben Reilly?

08:39.603 --> 08:42.730
Since Ruby died,
that's all I've thought about.

08:42.731 --> 08:46.401
Being just Ben Reilly.

08:49.321 --> 08:51.030
More coffee?

09:00.624 --> 09:02.668
Thank you, Thelma.

09:04.336 --> 09:06.045
You said he's an actor?

09:06.046 --> 09:07.755
We can call him Star Man.

09:07.756 --> 09:08.839
Aspiring actor.

09:08.840 --> 09:11.467
Still working his day job
as a subway driver.

09:11.468 --> 09:12.677
Subway driver?

09:12.678 --> 09:14.721
It's almost too good.

09:15.722 --> 09:17.014
The Conductor.

09:17.015 --> 09:18.392
Mm.

09:19.476 --> 09:21.727
It-It's electricity, he's a conductor.

09:21.728 --> 09:24.147
Oh, no, the issue wasn't one
of comprehension.

09:25.440 --> 09:26.607
You got photos?

09:26.608 --> 09:28.234
What do you think?

09:28.235 --> 09:32.281
Ah. I'll let the Bugle publish
my story on one condition.

09:32.864 --> 09:34.074
You'll let?

09:36.868 --> 09:38.578
Okay, calm down.

09:40.872 --> 09:42.082
What's the condition?

09:43.292 --> 09:46.253
You run my piece as is or not at all.

09:47.337 --> 09:49.505
Now, I need your word,
Walters, no changes.

09:49.506 --> 09:53.884
Unless, of course, you'd rather
I take this to the Herald.

09:53.885 --> 09:55.636
You got a lot of nerve,

09:55.637 --> 09:57.388
telling me how to do my job.

09:57.389 --> 09:58.389
What is that?

09:58.390 --> 09:59.725
Fine, sure, whatever you want.

10:02.311 --> 10:06.605
And I want the Bugle to print a retraction
about Lonnie Lincoln and Flint Marko.

10:06.606 --> 10:07.815
That's two conditions.

10:07.816 --> 10:09.025
Anything else?

10:09.026 --> 10:11.862
Well, now that you mention it...

10:32.591 --> 10:33.883
It's good to be back.

11:12.631 --> 11:14.048
Hey.

11:14.049 --> 11:15.425
Good to see you, too.

11:21.056 --> 11:23.933
So the prodigal son returned home, huh?

11:23.934 --> 11:26.102
Guess Silvermane took you back
with open arms.

11:26.103 --> 11:27.853
You can say what you want about him.

11:27.854 --> 11:29.480
That man takes care of his own.

11:29.481 --> 11:31.733
- One big happy family.
- Yeah.

11:32.734 --> 11:34.319
There's room for one more, brother.

11:34.903 --> 11:39.282
No offense, but I'm done putting
my life on the line for white men.

11:41.618 --> 11:44.412
It won't be like that, Lonnie.

11:44.413 --> 11:45.913
No?

11:45.914 --> 11:46.997
What, then?

11:46.998 --> 11:49.583
Silvermane want me to do his laundry?

11:49.584 --> 11:52.294
Or maybe he wants me to perform,
do a little hambone.

11:52.295 --> 11:53.754
You can't live like this forever, Lonnie.

11:53.755 --> 11:55.256
Buddy, with whatever's happening
inside us,

11:55.257 --> 11:57.341
I'm not too worried about living forever.

11:57.342 --> 11:59.677
All the more reason
we need to take what we can while we can.

11:59.678 --> 12:00.928
I'm not a criminal.

12:00.929 --> 12:03.222
Why don't you tell that
to the mayor or the cops?

12:03.223 --> 12:04.306
Take your pick.

12:04.307 --> 12:06.308
We're wanted men,
whether we like it or not.

12:06.309 --> 12:07.601
Do you think that's new to me?

12:07.602 --> 12:10.980
That's been my life
from the day I was born.

12:10.981 --> 12:12.189
Exactly.

12:12.190 --> 12:13.357
You risked your life for this country,

12:13.358 --> 12:15.651
and they still treat you
like a second-class citizen.

12:15.652 --> 12:20.531
Look, you said so yourself, we ain't
gonna make it to the retirement home,

12:20.532 --> 12:24.703
so let's take life by the balls while
we still have a little life left in us.

12:25.787 --> 12:27.330
Hear Silvermane out.

12:27.914 --> 12:29.374
That's all I'm asking.

12:45.056 --> 12:46.140
You've been busy.

12:46.141 --> 12:48.350
Yeah, someone's got to do
the work around here.

12:48.351 --> 12:49.685
Here, take a look at these.

12:49.686 --> 12:54.565
Four veterans, all from the same POW camp,
all with superhuman powers.

12:54.566 --> 12:56.734
Apparently the Germans
were doing experiments on them.

12:56.735 --> 12:59.863
Some kind of failed super soldier program.

13:01.865 --> 13:04.450
I'm sorry, are we boring you?

13:04.451 --> 13:06.327
The war ended 15 years ago.

13:06.328 --> 13:08.954
The question isn't what happened
to them then.

13:08.955 --> 13:11.957
The question is:
why are they getting their powers now?

13:11.958 --> 13:13.459
- Ah.
- Oh.

13:13.460 --> 13:14.543
That's why he...

13:14.544 --> 13:16.253
- that's why he does what he...
- That's, that's why he's...

13:16.254 --> 13:17.421
that's why his name's on the door.

13:17.422 --> 13:18.631
-  It's-it's on the door.
- I know.

13:18.632 --> 13:20.049
- I didn't do my homework, you know.
- Me neither. I don't...

13:20.050 --> 13:21.885
Well, is that supposed to mean
you know something?

13:22.469 --> 13:23.552
We do.

13:23.553 --> 13:25.346
Uh, are you going to share it?

13:25.347 --> 13:26.931
- Are you gonna be a dick about it?
- Uh, yes,

13:26.932 --> 13:29.558
actually, a private dick, to be exact.

13:29.559 --> 13:33.354
Okay. They were all seeing the same doctor
at the VA hospital in Queens.

13:33.355 --> 13:37.191
The doctor's been running a study
for the past ten years on POWs.

13:37.192 --> 13:42.613
According to Lonnie, it was specifically
about what happened to them in France.

13:42.614 --> 13:45.699
You know, I keep telling you, you'd make
an ace reporter if you ever want to...

13:45.700 --> 13:47.159
ditch the stiff.

13:47.160 --> 13:48.744
I have submitted a few applications.

13:48.745 --> 13:50.789
So this doctor's our guy?

13:51.373 --> 13:55.000
She is a geneticist--
Alethea Faber--

13:55.001 --> 13:56.085
one of the top in the country.

13:56.086 --> 13:59.713
Degrees from Stanford and Cornell,
I mean, every accolade you could imagine.

13:59.714 --> 14:03.717
All that, and she chooses to work
at a VA hospital in Queens,

14:03.718 --> 14:06.845
and according to Lonnie,
she sought them out

14:06.846 --> 14:09.558
nine months ago, knew all about the camp.

14:10.642 --> 14:12.185
What the hell are we waiting for?

14:13.478 --> 14:16.689
You, asshole, we were waiting on you.

14:16.690 --> 14:18.107
Well, then let's go, Robbie.

14:18.108 --> 14:20.569
-  You're welcome.
-  Don't rush me now, man.

14:22.862 --> 14:25.739
Lights out, boys.

14:36.793 --> 14:39.713
This place have
a cafeteria or something?

14:44.259 --> 14:45.885
Hey.

14:46.469 --> 14:48.262
Where's mine?

14:48.263 --> 14:49.764
Cut the shit, Leyden.

14:50.348 --> 14:52.433
We can go all night if you want to.

14:52.434 --> 14:55.519
Hey, I wonder, when's the last time
you said that to your wife, huh?

14:55.520 --> 14:57.605
Or her to you?
Never, I'm guessing.

14:59.941 --> 15:01.442
Ha!

15:05.113 --> 15:07.364
Do you have any cream or sugar?

15:07.365 --> 15:08.365
Yeah, I got some cream and sugar.

15:14.456 --> 15:16.707
Now I'm going to ask you again.

15:16.708 --> 15:20.753
Where did you
and your freak show friends...

15:20.754 --> 15:22.339
come from?

15:25.800 --> 15:27.718
A-All right.

15:27.719 --> 15:29.428
All right, I'll tell you, okay?

15:29.429 --> 15:30.471
Mm-hmm.

15:30.472 --> 15:34.267
I can't speak for the rest of 'em,
but me...

15:35.393 --> 15:36.686
...I'm from Poughkeepsie.

15:39.439 --> 15:41.940
Oh, he's mad now.

15:41.941 --> 15:43.359
Yeah, I know that look.

15:43.360 --> 15:47.405
Hey, you know, you remind me a lot
of my father.

15:48.573 --> 15:49.573
Oh!

15:56.665 --> 15:58.374
Do you like this?

15:58.375 --> 15:59.376
I do.

16:03.755 --> 16:06.216
Little bit too modern for my taste.

16:10.220 --> 16:12.806
Slippery son of a bitch, that Spider.

16:14.307 --> 16:15.974
What's his angle anyway?

16:15.975 --> 16:20.355
Well, I'm sure he's just trying to get by,
same as any of us.

16:21.564 --> 16:22.648
Is that what you're doing?

16:22.649 --> 16:26.235
Just trying to get by?

16:26.236 --> 16:28.529
Looks like you're doing
a bit better than that.

16:28.530 --> 16:29.739
Wonder why.

16:30.824 --> 16:33.242
You feeling a little unappreciated, Finn?

16:33.243 --> 16:34.577
Well, maybe I am.

16:35.161 --> 16:38.831
Well, I give thanks every day, trust me.

16:38.832 --> 16:41.543
You know, I say a little prayer before bed
and everything.

16:42.127 --> 16:45.505
Well, you ought to start saying one
every morning you get to wake up.

16:47.132 --> 16:49.175
Winston isn't so lucky now, is he?

16:51.886 --> 16:52.887
Ah.

16:54.305 --> 16:55.724
There they are.

17:03.773 --> 17:05.816
I wasn't expecting you boys so soon.

17:05.817 --> 17:08.319
Lonnie, meet Mr. Byrne.

17:10.071 --> 17:11.406
It's a pleasure to meet you.

17:14.951 --> 17:17.036
Flint told me a lot about you.

17:19.122 --> 17:20.539
Welcome back.

17:20.540 --> 17:22.207
Wasn't sure what happened to you.

17:22.208 --> 17:23.459
You read the papers,
don't you?

17:23.460 --> 17:25.462
He's a whole new man.

17:25.962 --> 17:29.131
Should see him when he gets going.
Unstoppable.

17:29.132 --> 17:30.550
My new right hand.

17:31.134 --> 17:35.679
Don't worry, boss, nothing's gonna happen
to you on my watch.

17:35.680 --> 17:38.682
Well, then, I guess,
congratulations on your promotion.

17:38.683 --> 17:40.434
I'm sure you'll make a wonderful couple.

17:42.353 --> 17:44.813
Don't mind her.
She's full of piss and vinegar today.

17:44.814 --> 17:47.984
Alas, I have to talk business
with the boys.

17:48.568 --> 17:51.820
Well, then I'll make my excuses.

17:51.821 --> 17:54.281
There's some paint upstairs
I can watch dry.

17:54.282 --> 17:58.535
Well, if you're so bored,
maybe you could find us a new band.

17:58.536 --> 18:01.206
Ah, one who knows the classics.

18:03.082 --> 18:07.504
And while you're at it,
look into another singer.

18:08.004 --> 18:11.674
Someone... young.

18:16.679 --> 18:19.057
Piss and vinegar.

18:24.437 --> 18:26.439
Hey, ma'am, how's it going?

18:28.566 --> 18:30.443
Must be some book.

18:31.945 --> 18:34.030
Is Dr. Faber in?

18:34.614 --> 18:36.115
You have an appointment?

18:36.950 --> 18:38.284
I do not.

18:39.494 --> 18:42.538
Joe Robertson, reporter with the Bugle.

18:42.539 --> 18:44.332
Just want to ask her a few questions.

18:48.419 --> 18:50.462
I'll let her office know you're here.

18:50.463 --> 18:52.298
If you would be so kind.

18:55.218 --> 18:57.636
You know, Paul dies in the end.

19:19.659 --> 19:22.704
There's a reporter downstairs
from the Daily Bugle.

19:24.831 --> 19:26.290
Robertson.

19:26.291 --> 19:28.376
He's asking to speak with you.

19:49.063 --> 19:51.316
Mr. Robertson?

19:51.900 --> 19:53.483
I'm Alethea Faber.

19:53.484 --> 19:54.903
Pleasure to meet you.

19:55.486 --> 19:57.029
And you are?

19:57.030 --> 19:58.489
What exactly did you want
to talk to me about?

19:59.073 --> 20:02.577
Don't suppose you saw my story
in the Bugle this morning.

20:03.161 --> 20:05.203
It'll just be a couple of minutes
of your time.

20:05.204 --> 20:07.873
Maybe spread the word
about the work you're doing.

20:07.874 --> 20:09.291
That can't be a bad thing, right?

20:09.292 --> 20:10.584
Let's speak outside.

20:39.072 --> 20:41.073
What can you tell me
about those men?

20:41.074 --> 20:42.741
Unfortunately, Mr. Robertson,

20:42.742 --> 20:45.327
we sent a great many men off to that war,

20:45.328 --> 20:49.373
and almost all of them came back with
injuries, either physical or spiritual.

20:49.374 --> 20:52.250
It's hard to remember all the patients
you've seen over the years.

20:52.251 --> 20:53.752
Well, I hope
that doesn't make me sound callous.

20:53.753 --> 20:55.838
Oh, no, no, no, no, of course not.

20:56.506 --> 20:58.924
It also doesn't make me
believe you.

20:58.925 --> 21:00.717
Are you calling her a liar?

21:00.718 --> 21:03.345
I'm sorry, sir,
I still haven't caught your name.

21:03.346 --> 21:04.805
This is my secretary Ogden.

21:04.806 --> 21:09.851
He has been with me for quite some time,
and he can be a bit overprotective.

21:09.852 --> 21:13.063
No, I can respect that,
but you're a smart woman.

21:13.064 --> 21:16.566
Do you really expect me to believe
you had no idea

21:16.567 --> 21:20.779
that four of your patients turned out
to have...

21:20.780 --> 21:22.699
superpowers?

21:24.951 --> 21:25.910
Or why?

21:26.494 --> 21:30.789
You are obviously a very intelligent man
yourself, Mr. Robertson,

21:30.790 --> 21:35.085
so you know that I'm not at liberty
to discuss specific patient information

21:35.086 --> 21:36.253
with anyone but the police.

21:36.254 --> 21:37.337
Well, have you done that?

21:37.338 --> 21:38.839
Have you spoken with the police?

21:38.840 --> 21:40.424
I am sorry, I cannot help you.

21:40.425 --> 21:42.092
Hmm.

21:42.093 --> 21:43.427
Did you help those men?

21:43.428 --> 21:48.224
You know, I'm hearing their powers only
started after they started seeing you.

21:51.060 --> 21:53.854
How dare you?
How dare you?

21:53.855 --> 21:56.648
To come here knowing nothing
and then accuse me

21:56.649 --> 21:59.401
of negligence in my care?

21:59.402 --> 22:03.363
Everything I do, I do for a reason.

22:03.364 --> 22:04.365
Everything.

22:08.286 --> 22:10.203
Struck a nerve, huh?

23:01.255 --> 23:02.964
Too much.

23:02.965 --> 23:03.841
This isn't good.

23:05.176 --> 23:07.427
All right, so what-what-what do we do?

23:07.428 --> 23:08.845
Calm down, Ogden.

23:08.846 --> 23:10.514
What do we do?

23:10.515 --> 23:11.849
Shut the door.

23:14.602 --> 23:17.187
He's a Negro.
Maybe no one will believe him.

23:17.188 --> 23:18.773
I don't think so.

23:21.984 --> 23:25.070
Hey, Dr. Collins,
where the hell have you been?

23:25.071 --> 23:27.155
I'm losing my mind back here.

23:27.156 --> 23:31.076
Hey, you're not Collins.

23:31.077 --> 23:32.327
What's going on?

23:32.328 --> 23:34.872
No, Dr. Collins
is on the second floor.

23:35.957 --> 23:37.542
The second floor?

23:38.584 --> 23:39.627
The second floor?

23:40.128 --> 23:42.796
The second floor? The second floor?

23:42.797 --> 23:45.465
All right, Ogden, could you please escort
this gentleman downstairs

23:45.466 --> 23:46.633
to Dr. Collins' office?

23:46.634 --> 23:48.510
The second floor.

23:48.511 --> 23:50.471
The second floor?

23:51.055 --> 23:52.681
The second floor.

23:52.682 --> 23:55.434
You don't like me very much.

23:59.647 --> 24:02.149
I know that man.

24:02.150 --> 24:03.275
What are you talking about?

24:03.276 --> 24:07.571
He was... there in France.

24:07.572 --> 24:09.657
He was the one who rescued us.

24:10.741 --> 24:12.076
It's him.

24:17.623 --> 24:19.792
Stop him. Go.

24:26.799 --> 24:28.383
Would you hurry up?

24:28.384 --> 24:29.885
I'm trying.

24:29.886 --> 24:32.263
See, this must be
one of them two-man jobs.

24:37.268 --> 24:38.352
Okay.

24:54.118 --> 24:56.119
Betty Botta bought...

24:56.120 --> 24:58.288
Betty bought a bit o' butter

24:58.289 --> 25:00.874
to make her butter batter better.

25:00.875 --> 25:03.002
Betty bought a bit o' batter.

25:03.502 --> 25:07.547
Betty bought a better butter,
makes the better batter better.

25:07.548 --> 25:09.799
Betty bought a better butter,
will make the batter better.

25:09.800 --> 25:11.259
Hey, pal.

25:11.260 --> 25:13.845
Shut it, huh?

25:13.846 --> 25:15.805
Betty bought a better batch

25:15.806 --> 25:17.641
of better butter.

25:17.642 --> 25:20.311
Betty bought a better batch
of better butter...

25:47.838 --> 25:48.839
Shit.

25:58.641 --> 26:00.017
You good?

26:02.061 --> 26:03.854
This was a new suit.

26:05.940 --> 26:07.441
Shit!

26:11.612 --> 26:13.405
Hark.

26:13.406 --> 26:16.324
What sound doth yonder bring?

26:16.325 --> 26:19.327
What do you think, bub, huh?

26:19.328 --> 26:21.079
Sounds like little peashooters to me.

26:21.080 --> 26:22.205
Shut up, Leyden.

26:22.206 --> 26:25.125
Cry "Havoc," my friends...

26:25.126 --> 26:28.128
and let loose the dogs of war.

27:02.997 --> 27:05.081
Well, what are you waiting for?

27:05.082 --> 27:06.083
Run.

27:12.840 --> 27:16.510
Please, please don't hurt me.

27:29.774 --> 27:31.066
Howdy, boys.

27:31.067 --> 27:32.902
Long time no see.

28:04.975 --> 28:07.519
Thought visiting hours was over.

28:07.520 --> 28:11.398
Mr. Leyden, that was quite the show
you put on last night.

28:11.399 --> 28:13.483
Oh, thank you, thank you.

28:13.484 --> 28:16.403
You know, I'd offer you an autograph,
but I don't have a pen.

28:17.488 --> 28:19.531
I assume you know who I am.

28:19.532 --> 28:22.410
The man with the mane of silver.

28:23.244 --> 28:25.245
Born from nothing.

28:25.246 --> 28:29.165
Built his empire through gut and guile.

28:29.166 --> 28:32.752
Purveyor of the finest prohibited potions.

28:32.753 --> 28:35.839
King of the five boroughs,

28:35.840 --> 28:41.303
Mr. Finbar Byrne himself-ah.

28:44.557 --> 28:46.516
I see you like to talk.

28:46.517 --> 28:48.184
Think you could listen for a second?

28:48.185 --> 28:53.064
Oh, I am, uh, like a Nebraskan cornfield.

28:53.065 --> 28:54.400
All ears.

28:57.445 --> 28:58.695
I'm listening.

28:58.696 --> 29:02.157
Mayor Morris appears to have forgotten
who runs this town.

29:02.158 --> 29:05.034
My men and I are planning to remind him.

29:05.035 --> 29:06.870
I want you to help me.

29:06.871 --> 29:08.621
Me?

29:08.622 --> 29:15.211
Oh, well, my only regret is
that I have but one life to give you.

29:15.212 --> 29:17.505
But I promise you,

29:17.506 --> 29:19.800
I will take plenty.

29:22.928 --> 29:24.305
Get him out of there.

29:26.098 --> 29:27.308
Ah.

29:32.396 --> 29:34.440
Oh, yes.

29:35.024 --> 29:37.109
Thank you, comrade.

29:44.283 --> 29:45.576
Please.

29:46.619 --> 29:47.952
I was just doing my job.

29:47.953 --> 29:53.374
Oh, and now I'm going to do mine.

29:56.253 --> 29:58.588
Life is but a walking shadow,

29:58.589 --> 30:00.590
a poor player

30:00.591 --> 30:03.760
that struts and frets his hour
upon the stage

30:03.761 --> 30:05.512
- and is heard no more.
- Please...

30:05.513 --> 30:08.598
A tale is told by an idiot,

30:08.599 --> 30:11.684
full of sound and fury.

30:11.685 --> 30:13.938
- No, no, no.
- Ah!

30:23.197 --> 30:25.324
And scene.

30:31.956 --> 30:34.040
That was weird.

30:34.041 --> 30:35.708
"Prisoners were injected

30:35.709 --> 30:39.504
with radiated plants and minerals
and the genetic material

30:39.505 --> 30:42.298
of spiders, scorpions, snakes..."

30:42.299 --> 30:45.051
Eels, too.

30:45.052 --> 30:46.219
Mm-hmm.

30:46.220 --> 30:48.471
"The Germans then altered
the subjects' genes

30:48.472 --> 30:52.016
by splicing them
with those of other entities.

30:52.017 --> 30:55.603
Over time, the patients' genetic material
began to decay.

30:55.604 --> 30:58.273
Many suffered lethal mutations

30:58.274 --> 31:03.236
while others survived in an altered state
for months or years."

31:03.237 --> 31:06.406
Faber has been looking for a cure,
but all she's managed to do

31:06.407 --> 31:08.700
is activate latent mutations

31:08.701 --> 31:10.076
and accelerate them.

31:10.077 --> 31:13.204
She's trying to save 'em,
but she's killing 'em.

31:13.205 --> 31:15.415
- The guy that bit you.
- Yeah.

31:15.416 --> 31:17.500
He was dying.

31:17.501 --> 31:19.253
But I lived.

31:19.837 --> 31:21.671
Why?

31:23.090 --> 31:24.341
Hmm.

31:27.845 --> 31:31.890
A doctor making monsters
in a secret lab in the Bronx.

31:32.391 --> 31:34.350
It's gonna make for one hell of a story.

31:34.351 --> 31:36.020
Hmm, first Black Pulitzer?

31:36.604 --> 31:38.646
Well, it's got to happen someday.

31:38.647 --> 31:40.231
Robbie, I have a request.

31:40.232 --> 31:41.190
Anything.

31:41.191 --> 31:42.609
Let me tell Cat before you print it.

31:42.610 --> 31:44.110
If Flint's gonna die because of this,

31:44.111 --> 31:46.614
I don't want her to read about it
in a newspaper.

31:47.615 --> 31:49.073
I said anything, didn't I?

31:54.830 --> 31:56.372
I'll give you a day.

31:56.373 --> 31:57.749
But I ain't losing this story.

31:57.750 --> 31:58.709
Deal.

32:00.127 --> 32:01.378
So...

32:02.212 --> 32:03.380
...how bad is it?

32:03.964 --> 32:07.217
How deep are you in with her?

32:07.801 --> 32:10.303
I suppose you're gonna tell me
to be careful.

32:10.304 --> 32:11.429
Oh, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

32:11.430 --> 32:15.266
Careful's for, um, for stock tips
and hot sauce.

32:15.267 --> 32:17.727
Matters of the heart, I say

32:17.728 --> 32:20.813
go for broke or don't bother going at all.

32:20.814 --> 32:22.273
Go for broke, huh?

32:24.276 --> 32:25.401
Wouldn't take much.

32:30.532 --> 32:31.741
Reilly.

32:50.511 --> 32:51.761
Mr. Reilly,

32:51.762 --> 32:52.930
take a seat.

32:54.932 --> 32:56.808
Can I get you anything?

32:56.809 --> 32:58.351
Glass of the good stuff?

32:58.352 --> 33:00.020
A perfect host.

33:04.775 --> 33:08.069
I take it you recognize my new associates.

33:08.070 --> 33:09.987
I read the papers.
Congratulations.

33:09.988 --> 33:13.408
You've assembled
an entire outfield of freaks.

33:13.409 --> 33:15.785
You guys see that movie Freaks
directed by Tod Browning?

33:15.786 --> 33:16.869
Still playing.

33:16.870 --> 33:20.039
You three could sign up for the remake.

33:20.040 --> 33:21.582
Calm down.

33:21.583 --> 33:25.962
Mr. Reilly is a little wise,
but we're all friends here, right?

33:25.963 --> 33:27.088
Yeah, sure.

33:27.089 --> 33:29.716
So, in the spirit
of friendship,

33:29.717 --> 33:33.136
I want to give you a chance
to warn The Spider...

33:33.137 --> 33:35.847
that this fight is between me and Morris,

33:35.848 --> 33:39.392
and if he gets his nose in my business,
he's liable to lose it.

33:39.393 --> 33:40.602
Is that clear?

33:41.186 --> 33:43.479
As a bell.
Is that all?

33:43.480 --> 33:48.067
I don't mean to be rude,
but, uh, I've got theater tickets.

33:48.068 --> 33:49.569
You ever been on Broadway?

33:49.570 --> 33:52.196
No? Probably drove a train
underneath it, though, right?

33:52.197 --> 33:54.824
Mr. To Be or Not to Be.

33:54.825 --> 33:57.493
♪ Camera's rolling, the lights are on ♪

33:57.494 --> 34:01.164
♪ The director calls "Action,"
the director calls "Cut" ♪

34:01.165 --> 34:03.624
♪ Mr. Leyden, Dirk ♪

34:05.502 --> 34:06.878
Tell your friend

34:06.879 --> 34:10.883
it's in all our best interests
to play nice.

34:12.718 --> 34:13.927
You got it.

34:25.230 --> 34:26.814
Hey.

34:26.815 --> 34:29.859
I hear you make all the ladies faint.

34:29.860 --> 34:31.236
Make me faint.

34:32.946 --> 34:34.822
I know about Winston.

34:34.823 --> 34:36.324
My condolences.

34:36.325 --> 34:38.159
Were you two close?

34:38.160 --> 34:42.414
I know you set him up, Reilly,
and I know you did it for her.

34:46.126 --> 34:48.002
Her?

34:48.003 --> 34:49.630
Don't take me for dumb.

34:50.214 --> 34:53.216
I didn't tell the boss
'cause he would've killed the both of you.

34:53.217 --> 34:55.384
And mad as I am, I don't want Cat dead.

34:58.680 --> 35:00.473
You okay, pal?

35:00.474 --> 35:02.017
You look pretty rough.

35:03.769 --> 35:05.145
I'm fine.

35:05.979 --> 35:09.565
You keep doing Silvermane's dirty work,
and maybe you won't be.

35:09.566 --> 35:11.819
You worry about yourself, Reilly.

35:13.695 --> 35:16.697
You get one pass because you saved her.

35:16.698 --> 35:18.659
This is it.

35:21.954 --> 35:23.579
You know...

35:24.706 --> 35:29.252
...a hot dog at the game is better
than roast beef at the Ritz.

35:29.253 --> 35:30.504
Think about it.

35:43.225 --> 35:45.476
Now we've got no secrets,
you're done with the stairs?

35:45.477 --> 35:47.812
I didn't want to be seen.

35:47.813 --> 35:49.439
Flint's back with Silvermane.

35:50.190 --> 35:51.607
I know.

35:51.608 --> 35:53.150
I saw him this morning.

35:53.151 --> 35:54.777
Acted like he didn't even know me.

35:54.778 --> 35:57.072
And that bothered you?

35:59.783 --> 36:01.993
You swooped in here to ask me that?

36:01.994 --> 36:03.369
He knows you tried to kill Silvermane.

36:03.370 --> 36:05.288
He heard us talking the other night.

36:05.289 --> 36:07.081
- And has he told him?
- He doesn't want to see you dead.

36:07.082 --> 36:08.958
He's not well, Ben, I'm worried about him.

36:08.959 --> 36:10.084
You should be.

36:18.677 --> 36:20.928
You can spare me the dramatic pause.

36:20.929 --> 36:22.013
Whatever it is, I can take it.

36:22.014 --> 36:23.806
Flint and some of the other guys
in that camp

36:23.807 --> 36:26.601
have been seeing a doctor at the VA,
a woman called Faber.

36:26.602 --> 36:29.437
She's been trying to come up with a cure,
but she's only made them worse.

36:29.438 --> 36:30.438
What do you mean, worse?

36:30.439 --> 36:34.109
What the Germans did will eventually
kill them, but she's speeding it up.

36:35.193 --> 36:36.653
You mean Flint's gonna die?

36:43.035 --> 36:44.118
When?

36:44.119 --> 36:48.624
All I know is, every time he uses
his powers, he gets a little closer.

36:49.833 --> 36:52.376
- Thank you for telling me.
- Cat.

36:52.377 --> 36:54.211
He says one word, and we're both dead.

36:54.212 --> 36:56.048
I'd like to be alone, please.

37:05.098 --> 37:07.600
What's left for us here?

37:07.601 --> 37:10.728
Ruby's gone, Flint's past helping.

37:10.729 --> 37:12.813
We're chasing ghosts.

37:12.814 --> 37:14.858
But you and I could have something.

37:15.901 --> 37:19.403
What if we left New York,
went someplace where nobody knows us?

37:19.404 --> 37:21.280
What was that island with the black sand?

37:21.281 --> 37:22.281
Santorini.

37:22.282 --> 37:23.532
Santorini. We could go there,

37:23.533 --> 37:26.244
wherever you want,
you could open your own club.

37:26.995 --> 37:28.079
What about you?

37:28.080 --> 37:29.747
Well, I'll run it or bartend.

37:29.748 --> 37:31.457
I'll work for you.

37:31.458 --> 37:35.628
I don't know what this is, but I do know,
for the first time in years

37:35.629 --> 37:38.006
I'm willing to take a chance and find out.

37:40.926 --> 37:41.927
Okay.

37:42.511 --> 37:43.595
Okay?

37:45.931 --> 37:47.014
Okay.

37:57.943 --> 38:00.861
I'll have the, uh, the, uh...

38:00.862 --> 38:02.738
ooh, I'll have the hot dog deluxe.

38:02.739 --> 38:05.866
You know what? No, no,
I'll just have a scoop of cottage cheese.

38:05.867 --> 38:07.535
Cottage cheese?

38:07.536 --> 38:08.828
You on a diet or something?

38:08.829 --> 38:10.162
There might be a beach in my future.

38:10.163 --> 38:13.040
Oh, and breakfast is on me,
so you should have at it.

38:13.041 --> 38:14.500
Okay, now I'm really confused.

38:14.501 --> 38:16.669
Uh, uh, scrambled eggs, bacon.

38:16.670 --> 38:18.004
They've got New York cheesecake.

38:18.005 --> 38:20.465
- I was just gonna...
- Just bring it all.

38:21.466 --> 38:25.136
♪ I love cheesecake ♪

38:25.137 --> 38:28.389
♪ in the morning ♪

38:28.390 --> 38:31.851
♪ with you ♪

38:31.852 --> 38:33.269
Okay, well, that's new.

38:33.270 --> 38:34.770
Never heard you sing.

38:34.771 --> 38:35.730
Didn't even know you knew how.

38:35.731 --> 38:37.232
There's a lot you don't know about me.

38:38.025 --> 38:39.108
Is there?

38:39.109 --> 38:41.777
You'd be surprised.

38:41.778 --> 38:43.155
Would I?

38:43.739 --> 38:45.865
You know, your hair looks lovely,
by the way.

38:45.866 --> 38:46.949
Did you curl it?

38:46.950 --> 38:48.034
Three weeks ago.

38:48.035 --> 38:49.326
Now spill it.

38:51.329 --> 38:52.496
Oh, boy.

38:52.497 --> 38:53.498
What?

38:54.916 --> 38:56.334
I'm leaving town.

38:57.586 --> 38:58.669
Permanently?

38:58.670 --> 39:02.256
I think so, yeah, but don't worry,
I promise you'll be taken care of.

39:02.257 --> 39:03.215
What about the office?

39:03.216 --> 39:05.092
Well, get rid of it or keep it.

39:05.093 --> 39:07.679
You're a better P.I.
than I am anyway, so...

39:10.265 --> 39:12.349
I'll be damned.

39:12.350 --> 39:13.894
It's Cat, isn't it?

39:17.022 --> 39:18.439
Yes...

39:18.440 --> 39:19.982
It-it sounds crazy,

39:19.983 --> 39:22.318
- I know, crazy, crazy, crazy...
- Ben--

39:22.319 --> 39:24.320
...because we've only known
each other for a few weeks,

39:24.321 --> 39:27.239
but if it took Cat to drag me
out of this hole that I've been hiding in,

39:27.240 --> 39:29.158
well, then I owe it to both of us
to see it through...

39:29.159 --> 39:30.326
- Ben--
- ...because this is the first time

39:30.327 --> 39:31.827
in-in years that I feel alive.

39:31.828 --> 39:33.329
- For Christ's sake--
- I mean... with the matters of the heart,

39:33.330 --> 39:34.246
you got to go for broke.

39:34.247 --> 39:35.664
- Ben, Ben--
- Robbie says that you just got...

39:35.665 --> 39:37.334
- With matters of the heart, you got...
- Oh, for Christ's sake, Ben!

39:40.587 --> 39:42.589
I'm really happy for you.

39:43.548 --> 39:44.632
You are?

39:44.633 --> 39:45.925
Yes.

39:45.926 --> 39:47.927
♪ What you lack ♪

39:47.928 --> 39:50.888
♪ Better get yourself some jive, Jack ♪

39:50.889 --> 39:53.641
♪ Lay back and let yourself relax ♪

39:53.642 --> 39:56.394
♪ Leave everything to Mr. Rhythm ♪

40:25.882 --> 40:27.174
Who is it?

40:27.175 --> 40:28.676
Lonnie Lincoln, ma'am.

40:28.677 --> 40:30.594
I need to talk to you.

40:30.595 --> 40:32.013
It's about Flint.

41:04.045 --> 41:06.130
Don't.

41:06.131 --> 41:07.214
Flint.

41:07.215 --> 41:08.257
- Don't.
- Please, Flint.

41:08.258 --> 41:09.675
- Don't.
- Let me take a look at you.

41:09.676 --> 41:11.594
It's getting worse.

41:11.595 --> 41:13.262
- I just want to help.
- You've done enough, don't you think?

41:13.263 --> 41:15.431
Silvermane will never let us be together.

41:15.432 --> 41:17.433
What I did, I did for us.

41:17.434 --> 41:18.809
Without telling me?

41:18.810 --> 41:20.644
- Why, because I'm stupid?
- No.

41:20.645 --> 41:22.354
I'm just a meathead
with his brains in his fists?

41:22.355 --> 41:25.191
No, I didn't tell you
because I knew you would say no.

41:25.192 --> 41:27.943
And how do you think
it makes me feel, Flint,

41:27.944 --> 41:30.654
that you're more loyal to that man
than you are to me,

41:30.655 --> 41:35.075
that you'd have me living under his thumb,
unable to breathe without his say-so?

41:35.076 --> 41:37.286
That's funny to you?

41:37.287 --> 41:39.414
No, what's funny is,
I would've killed him for you.

41:40.373 --> 41:43.000
I would've done anything for you
if you'd just asked,

41:43.001 --> 41:44.544
but you never gave me the chance.

41:45.462 --> 41:46.754
But why would you?

41:46.755 --> 41:50.091
I'm nothing but muscle
for a gangster, huh?

41:51.801 --> 41:55.931
Well, maybe it's time I accepted that,
leaned into it.

41:58.642 --> 42:00.143
Ain't that right, Lonnie?

42:01.228 --> 42:04.939
You and me, buddy,
about to die in a blaze of goddamn glory.

42:04.940 --> 42:06.815
- Flint, please.
- Stay away from me.

42:06.816 --> 42:08.276
- Please!
- Stay away!

42:21.665 --> 42:23.458
- Flint.
- Let him go.

42:35.512 --> 42:37.638
This Faber woman.

42:37.639 --> 42:39.391
She really couldn't help you?

42:40.809 --> 42:42.435
There's really no hope?

42:45.021 --> 42:47.356
Faber said there's only one thing
left to try.

42:48.650 --> 42:50.652
But she couldn't make it happen.

42:52.654 --> 42:53.989
What was it?

42:55.031 --> 42:56.408
Not what.

42:57.409 --> 42:58.493
Who.

43:01.329 --> 43:02.664
The Spider.

43:04.291 --> 43:05.458
Why?

43:08.169 --> 43:09.838
Why would he change things?

43:10.338 --> 43:14.592
She thinks his mutation is different,
more stable than ours.

43:15.093 --> 43:18.262
She said he could be
the answer to all of this.

43:18.263 --> 43:20.807
Problem is, she's got no idea who he is...

43:22.017 --> 43:23.351
...or where to find him.

43:33.486 --> 43:34.570
We need to go.

43:34.571 --> 43:36.530
We have to clear the lab.

43:36.531 --> 43:38.115
Maybe it's not as bad as we think it is.

43:38.116 --> 43:40.242
No, we can't be naive.

43:41.328 --> 43:44.455
I mean, as soon as that reporter
publishes his story,

43:44.456 --> 43:45.998
they're coming for us.

43:45.999 --> 43:48.375
We can't just give up.

43:48.376 --> 43:52.296
You have done everything you could.

43:52.297 --> 43:54.715
Now it's time to go.

44:08.438 --> 44:10.230
All right, watch your step over here.

44:10.231 --> 44:11.523
Dr. Faber.

44:11.524 --> 44:13.442
I just want to know:

44:13.443 --> 44:17.237
if you find The Spider,
are you really able to help them?

44:17.238 --> 44:19.281
Flint, Lonnie, all of them?

44:19.282 --> 44:21.450
You know who The Spider is, don't you?

44:21.451 --> 44:25.746
If I tell you...
do you promise you won't hurt him?

44:25.747 --> 44:28.083
You have my word.

44:29.084 --> 44:30.502
His name...

44:32.545 --> 44:33.796
...is Ben Reilly.
